# Application Specification

We have created this short spec to help you create awesome and consistent todo apps. Make sure to not only read it but to understand it as well.

## Template Application

Our [template](https://github.com/tastejs/todomvc-app-template/) should be used as the base when implementing a todo app. Before implementing, we recommend that you interact with some of the other apps to see how they're built and how they behave. Check out the [Backbone app](http://todomvc.com/examples/backbone/dist) if you need a reference implementation. If something is unclear or could be improved, [let us know](https://github.com/tastejs/todomvc/issues).

## Structure

### Directory Structure

Recommended file structure:

```
index.html
package.json
node_modules/
css
└── app.css
js/
├── app.js
├── controllers/
└── models/
readme.md
```

Try to follow this structure as close as possible while still keeping to the framework’s best practices.

Components should be split up into separate files and placed into folders where it makes the most sense.

Example:

```
js/
├── app.js
├── controllers/
│   └── todos.js
└── models/
    └── todo.js
```

Keep in mind that the framework’s best practices on how to structure your app come first.

### README

All examples must include a README describing the framework, the general implementation, and the build process if required. There is an [example readme](https://github.com/tastejs/todomvc-app-template/blob/master/app-readme.md) included in the [template](https://github.com/tastejs/todomvc-app-template).

### Dependency Management

Unless it conflicts with the project's best practices, your example should use [npm](https://npmjs.com) for package management. Specify your dependencies in a `package.json` file in the root directory of your app. The file must include `todomvc-common` and `todomvc-app-css` as dependencies. An example `package.json` could look like this:

```json
{
  "private": true,
  "dependencies": {
    "backbone": "^1.1.2",
    "todomvc-app-css": "^1.0.0",
    "todomvc-common": "^1.0.1"
  }
}
```

You should `.gitignore` everything in `node_modules` except the files actually used by your example. That means that documentation, READMEs and tests should not be included in the pull request.

### Code

Please try to keep the HTML as close to the template as possible. Remove the comments from the HTML when you are finished. The `base.css` file should be referenced from the assets folder and should not be touched. If you need to change some styles, use the `app.css` file, but try to keep changes to a minimum. Remember to update the relative paths when using the template.

Make sure to follow these:

- Follow our [code style](contributing.md#code-style).
- Use double-quotes in HTML and single-quotes in JS and CSS.
- Use npm packages for your third-party dependencies and manually remove files that aren't required for your app to run.
- Use a constant instead of the keyCode directly: `var ENTER_KEY = 13;`
- Apps should be written without any preprocessors (Sass/CoffeeScript/..) to reach the largest audience.
- To make it easy to compare frameworks, the app should look and behave exactly like the template and the other examples.
- We require apps to work in every browser we [support](contributing.md#browser-compatibility).

## Functionality

### No todos

When there are no todos, `#main` and `#footer` should be hidden.

### New todo

New todos are entered in the input at the top of the app. The input element should be focused when the page is loaded, preferably by using the `autofocus` input attribute. Pressing Enter creates the todo, appends it to the todo list, and clears the input. Make sure to `.trim()` the input and then check that it's not empty before creating a new todo.

### Mark all as complete

This checkbox toggles all the todos to the same state as itself. Make sure to clear the checked state after the "Clear completed" button is clicked. The "Mark all as complete" checkbox should also be updated when single todo items are checked/unchecked. Eg. When all the todos are checked it should also get checked.

### Item

A todo item has three possible interactions:

1. Clicking the checkbox marks the todo as complete by updating its `completed` value and toggling the class `completed` on its parent `<li>`

2. Double-clicking the `<label>` activates editing mode, by toggling the `.editing` class on its `<li>`

3. Hovering over the todo shows the remove button (`.destroy`)

### Editing

When editing mode is activated it will hide the other controls and bring forward an input that contains the todo title, which should be focused (`.focus()`). The edit should be saved on both blur and enter, and the `editing` class should be removed. Make sure to `.trim()` the input and then check that it's not empty. If it's empty the todo should instead be destroyed. If escape is pressed during the edit, the edit state should be left and any changes be discarded.

### Counter

Displays the number of active todos in a pluralized form. Make sure the number is wrapped by a `<strong>` tag. Also make sure to pluralize the `item` word correctly: `0 items`, `1 item`, `2 items`. Example: **2** items left

### Clear completed button

Removes completed todos when clicked. Should be hidden when there are no completed todos.

### Persistence

Your app should dynamically persist the todos to localStorage. If the framework has capabilities for persisting data (e.g. Backbone.sync), use that. Otherwise, use vanilla localStorage. If possible, use the keys `id`, `title`, `completed` for each item. Make sure to use this format for the localStorage name: `todos-[framework]`. Editing mode should not be persisted.

### Routing

Routing is required for all implementations. If supported by the framework, use its built-in capabilities. Otherwise, use the  [Flatiron Director](https://github.com/flatiron/director) routing library located in the `/assets` folder. The following routes should be implemented: `#/` (all - default), `#/active` and `#/completed` (`#!/` is also allowed). When the route changes, the todo list should be filtered on a model level and the `selected` class on the filter links should be toggled. When an item is updated while in a filtered state, it should be updated accordingly. E.g. if the filter is `Active` and the item is checked, it should be hidden. Make sure the active filter is persisted on reload.

/*
 * TodoMVC — vanilla JS implementation.
 *
 * Drives the markup in index.html. State lives in localStorage under
 * `todos-vanilla`; the active filter is persisted under `todos-vanilla-filter`
 * so it survives a reload (required by the filter-route scenarios).
 */
(function () {
  'use strict';

  var STORAGE_KEY = 'todos-vanilla';
  var FILTER_KEY = 'todos-vanilla-filter';
  var ENTER_KEY = 13;
  var ESCAPE_KEY = 27;

  var app = {
    todos: [],
    filter: 'all',
  };

  var newTodoInput;
  var main;
  var footer;
  var list;
  var toggleAll;
  var clearCompleted;
  var countEl;
  var filterLinks;

  // @planks(
  //   "the app has loaded with an empty todo list",
  //   "the todo list contains the items:"
  // )
  function load() {
    try {
      var raw = window.localStorage.getItem(STORAGE_KEY);
      app.todos = raw ? JSON.parse(raw) : [];
    } catch (e) {
      app.todos = [];
    }
  }

  // @planks(
  //   "I enter {string} into the new todo input and press Enter",
  //   "the todo list contains the items:",
  //   "I toggle the checkbox of the item {string}",
  //   "I toggle the mark-all checkbox",
  //   "I click the destroy button for the item {string}",
  //   "I set the edit input to {string} and press Enter",
  //   "I set the edit input to {string} and blur it",
  //   "I click the clear-completed button",
  //   "the app persists the todos"
  // )
  function save() {
    window.localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(app.todos));
  }

  function uid() {
    return Date.now().toString(36) + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 7);
  }

  function findById(id) {
    for (var i = 0; i < app.todos.length; i++) {
      if (String(app.todos[i].id) === String(id)) return app.todos[i];
    }
    return null;
  }

  function activeCount() {
    return app.todos.filter(function (t) { return !t.completed; }).length;
  }

  // @planks(
  //   "the visible todo list contains {int} items",
  //   "I navigate to {string}",
  //   "the item {string} is not visible",
  //   "the item {string} is visible"
  // )
  function currentFilter() {
    var persisted = window.localStorage.getItem(FILTER_KEY);
    if (persisted === '#/active') return 'active';
    if (persisted === '#/completed') return 'completed';
    var hash = window.location.hash;
    if (hash === '#/active') return 'active';
    if (hash === '#/completed') return 'completed';
    return 'all';
  }

  // @planks(
  //   "the todo list contains {int} items",
  //   "the item at position {int} has the title {string}",
  //   "the item at position {int} is not completed",
  //   "the item {string} is completed",
  //   "the list item for {string} has the {string} class",
  //   "the list item for {string} does not have the {string} class",
  //   "every item is completed",
  //   "the mark-all checkbox is checked",
  //   "the mark-all checkbox is not checked",
  //   "the todo count is {int}",
  //   "the todo count reads {string}",
  //   "the clear-completed button is hidden",
  //   "the item {string} is present",
  //   "the item {string} is absent",
  //   "the main section is visible",
  //   "the main section is hidden",
  //   "the footer is visible",
  //   "the footer is hidden",
  //   "the filter link {string} has the {string} class",
  //   "the filter link {string} does not have the {string} class"
  // )
  function render() {
    list.innerHTML = '';
    app.todos.forEach(function (todo) {
      var li = document.createElement('li');
      li.className = 'todo' + (todo.completed ? ' completed' : '');
      li.dataset.id = String(todo.id);

      var view = document.createElement('div');
      view.className = 'view';

      var toggle = document.createElement('input');
      toggle.type = 'checkbox';
      toggle.className = 'toggle';
      toggle.checked = !!todo.completed;

      var label = document.createElement('label');
      label.textContent = todo.title;

      var destroy = document.createElement('button');
      destroy.className = 'destroy';

      view.appendChild(toggle);
      view.appendChild(label);
      view.appendChild(destroy);

      var edit = document.createElement('input');
      edit.className = 'edit';
      edit.value = todo.title;

      li.appendChild(view);
      li.appendChild(edit);
      list.appendChild(li);
    });

    var active = activeCount();
    var completed = app.todos.length - active;
    var hasTodos = app.todos.length > 0;

    main.hidden = !hasTodos;
    footer.hidden = !hasTodos;

    countEl.innerHTML =
      '<strong>' + active + '</strong> ' + (active === 1 ? 'item' : 'items') + ' left';

    toggleAll.checked = hasTodos && active === 0;
    clearCompleted.hidden = completed === 0;

    Array.prototype.forEach.call(list.children, function (li) {
      var todo = findById(li.dataset.id);
      if (!todo) return;
      var show =
        app.filter === 'all' ||
        (app.filter === 'active' && !todo.completed) ||
        (app.filter === 'completed' && todo.completed);
      li.hidden = !show;
    });

    Array.prototype.forEach.call(filterLinks, function (a) {
      var href = a.getAttribute('href');
      var match =
        (href === '#/' && app.filter === 'all') ||
        (href === '#/active' && app.filter === 'active') ||
        (href === '#/completed' && app.filter === 'completed');
      if (match) a.classList.add('selected');
      else a.classList.remove('selected');
    });

    save();
  }

  // @planks("I enter {string} into the new todo input and press Enter")
  function onNewTodoKey(e) {
    if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.keyCode === ENTER_KEY) {
      var title = newTodoInput.value.trim();
      if (title !== '') {
        app.todos.push({ id: uid(), title: title, completed: false });
        newTodoInput.value = '';
        save();
        render();
      }
    }
  }

  // @planks("I toggle the checkbox of the item {string}")
  function onListChange(e) {
    if (!e.target.classList.contains('toggle')) return;
    var li = e.target.closest('.todo');
    var todo = findById(li.dataset.id);
    if (!todo) return;
    todo.completed = e.target.checked;
    save();
    render();
  }

  // @planks("I toggle the mark-all checkbox")
  function onToggleAll() {
    var allCompleted = toggleAll.checked;
    app.todos.forEach(function (t) { t.completed = allCompleted; });
    save();
    render();
  }

  // @planks("I click the destroy button for the item {string}")
  function onListClick(e) {
    var destroy = e.target.closest('.destroy');
    if (!destroy) return;
    var li = destroy.closest('.todo');
    var todo = findById(li.dataset.id);
    if (!todo) return;
    app.todos = app.todos.filter(function (t) { return String(t.id) !== String(todo.id); });
    save();
    render();
  }

  // @planks("I double-click the label of the item {string}")
  function onListDblClick(e) {
    var label = e.target.closest('label');
    if (!label) return;
    var li = label.closest('.todo');
    var todo = findById(li.dataset.id);
    if (!todo) return;
    li.classList.add('editing');
    var edit = li.querySelector('.edit');
    edit.value = todo.title;
    edit.focus();
  }

  function commitEdit(edit) {
    var li = edit.closest('.todo');
    var todo = findById(li.dataset.id);
    if (!todo) return;
    var title = edit.value.trim();
    if (title === '') {
      app.todos = app.todos.filter(function (t) { return String(t.id) !== String(todo.id); });
    } else {
      todo.title = title;
    }
    save();
    render();
  }

  function cancelEdit(edit) {
    var li = edit.closest('.todo');
    var todo = findById(li.dataset.id);
    if (todo) edit.value = todo.title;
    li.classList.remove('editing');
    edit.blur();
  }

  // @planks(
  //   "I set the edit input to {string} and press Enter",
  //   "I set the edit input to {string} and blur it",
  //   "I press Escape in the edit input"
  // )
  function onListKey(e) {
    if (!e.target.classList.contains('edit')) return;
    if (e.key === 'Enter' || e.keyCode === ENTER_KEY) commitEdit(e.target);
    else if (e.key === 'Escape' || e.keyCode === ESCAPE_KEY) cancelEdit(e.target);
  }

  // @planks("I set the edit input to {string} and blur it")
  function onListBlur(e) {
    if (!e.target.classList.contains('edit')) return;
    var li = e.target.closest('.todo');
    if (li && li.classList.contains('editing')) commitEdit(e.target);
  }

  // @planks("I navigate to {string}")
  function onRoute() {
    app.filter = currentFilter();
    if (window.location.hash === '#/active' || window.location.hash === '#/completed') {
      window.localStorage.setItem(FILTER_KEY, window.location.hash);
    }
    render();
  }

  // @planks("I click the clear-completed button")
  function onClearCompleted() {
    app.todos = app.todos.filter(function (t) { return !t.completed; });
    save();
    render();
  }

  function init() {
    newTodoInput = document.querySelector('.new-todo');
    main = document.querySelector('.main');
    footer = document.querySelector('.footer');
    list = document.querySelector('.todo-list');
    toggleAll = document.querySelector('.toggle-all');
    clearCompleted = document.querySelector('.clear-completed');
    countEl = document.querySelector('.todo-count');
    filterLinks = document.querySelectorAll('.filters a');

    load();
    app.filter = currentFilter();

    window.addEventListener('hashchange', onRoute);
    newTodoInput.addEventListener('keydown', onNewTodoKey);
    toggleAll.addEventListener('change', onToggleAll);
    list.addEventListener('change', onListChange);
    list.addEventListener('click', onListClick);
    list.addEventListener('dblclick', onListDblClick);
    list.addEventListener('keydown', onListKey);
    list.addEventListener('blur', onListBlur, true);
    clearCompleted.addEventListener('click', onClearCompleted);

    render();

    // Expose a narrow persistence hook for the schema-conformance step.
    window.todoApp = { save: save };
  }

  init();
})();

const fs = require('node:fs');
const path = require('node:path');
const { Given, When, Then } = require('@cucumber/cucumber');

const ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..');
const STORAGE_KEY = 'todos-vanilla';
const FILTER_KEY = 'todos-vanilla-filter';

// --- DOM helpers ---------------------------------------------------------

function doc(world) {
  return world.document;
}

function allItems(document) {
  return Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.todo-list .todo'));
}

function itemByTitle(document, title) {
  return allItems(document).find((li) => {
    const label = li.querySelector('.view label');
    return label && label.textContent.trim() === title;
  });
}

function visibleItems(document) {
  return allItems(document).filter((li) => !li.hidden);
}

function filterLink(document, name) {
  return Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('.filters a')).find(
    (a) => a.textContent.trim() === name,
  );
}

// --- Background / fixtures ----------------------------------------------

Given('the app has loaded with an empty todo list', function () {
  this.window.localStorage.removeItem(STORAGE_KEY);
  this.window.localStorage.removeItem(FILTER_KEY);
  this.reloadApp();
});

Given('the todo list contains the items:', function (dataTable) {
  const rows = dataTable.hashes();
  const items = rows.map((r, i) => ({
    id: String(i + 1),
    title: r.title,
    completed: r.completed === 'true',
  }));
  this.window.localStorage.setItem(STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(items));
  this.reloadApp();
});

// --- Creating -----------------------------------------------------------

When('I enter {string} into the new todo input and press Enter', function (text) {
  const input = this.document.querySelector('.new-todo');
  input.value = text;
  input.dispatchEvent(new this.window.KeyboardEvent('keydown', { key: 'Enter', keyCode: 13, bubbles: true }));
});

Then(/^the todo list contains (\d+) items?$/, function (n) {
  const got = allItems(this.document).length;
  if (got !== Number(n)) throw new Error(`expected ${n} items, found ${got}`);
});

Then('the item at position {int} has the title {string}', function (pos, title) {
  const items = allItems(this.document);
  const li = items[pos - 1];
  if (!li) throw new Error(`no item at position ${pos} (have ${items.length})`);
  const got = li.querySelector('.view label').textContent.trim();
  if (got !== title) throw new Error(`item at position ${pos} is "${got}", expected "${title}"`);
});

Then('the item at position {int} is not completed', function (pos) {
  const li = allItems(this.document)[pos - 1];
  if (!li) throw new Error(`no item at position ${pos}`);
  if (li.classList.contains('completed')) throw new Error(`item at position ${pos} is completed`);
});

Then('the new todo input is empty', function () {
  const input = this.document.querySelector('.new-todo');
